{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558861-2nd-revised-v20-damage-soak-and-1s","id":1558861,"title":"[2nd, Revised, V20] Damage, Soak and 1s","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-14T18:32:08-07:00","id":1558861,"title":"[2nd, Revised, V20] Damage, Soak and 1s","content":"Direct question for the aforementioned editions: when you roll damage or soak, what do you do with dice that come up as 1?<br /> If you roll 7 dice for a difficulty 6 damage roll and get `5 6 9 3 1 4 6`, do you count that as 2 or 3 successes?<br /> <br /> This question arises from a reddit post (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/1rr68g2/comment/oaebzcn/\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>) in which a comment says &quot;1s do not count away from successes in damage or soak rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> After looking through the rulebooks in detail, I found that all the core rulebook say more or less the same: 1 subtract success on damage and soak. The only conflict information came from the &quot;V20 - Glossary&quot; that address the &quot;botch&quot; both as the die that came out as &quot;1&quot; and the result of the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>2nd Edition</b><ul><li>p77: General Rule: Whenever you roll a one, it cancels out a success. It completely takes it away. You remove both the \u201csuccess\u201ddie and the \u201cone\u201d die and pay them no more heed. If you roll more ones than you do successes, a disaster occurs; something called a botch takes place. Don\u2019t count the ones that canceled out successes, but if evenasingle one is left after all the successes have been canceled, a botch occurs.</li> <li>p83: Glossary: A disastrous failure, indicated by rolling more ones than successes on the 10-sided dice rolled for an action.</li> <li>p224: Combat system: Damage and soak rolls are the only rolls in Vampire which cannot be botched.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Revised</b><ul><li>p192: General Rule: if none of your dice comes up a success, and there are dice showing \u201c1s\u201d (no matter how many), the roll is a botch. If you score at least one success, even if that success is canceled out and additional \u201c1s\u201d remain, it\u2019s just a simple failure.</li> <li>p208: Combat system - Damage: Moreover a damage effect rolls cannot botch; a botched roll simply means the attack glances harmlessly off the target.</li> <li>p209: Combat system - Soak: Example: Liselle the Gangrel has Stamina 3 and Fortitude 1. She is attacked with a knife, and the attacker scores three levels of lethal damage. Liselle may soak this attack with four dice (Stamina 3 + Fortitude 1). She rolls 1 , 9 , 9 , 7.The \u201c1\u201d cancels out one of the Successes, leaving Liselle with two. She thus ignores two of the three health levels inflicted by the knife, taking only one level of damage.</li> </ul><br /> <b>V20</b><ul><li>p250: General Rule: If none of your dice comes up a success, and one or more dice are dice showing 1, the roll is a botch. If you score at least one success, even if that success is canceled out and additional 1s remain, it\u2019s just a simple failure.</li> <li>p272: Combat system - Damage: Moreover, damage effect rolls cannot botch; a botched roll simply means the attack glances harmlessly off the target.</li> <li>p274: Combat system - Soak: As with damage rolls, soak rolls may not botch, only fail.</li> <li>p306: Example of play: &quot;Jillian attempts to soak and fails outright, rolling 4, 1, 9.&quot;</li> <li>p513: Glossary: Botch: 1) A naturally rolled 1, which cancels out a success die. 2) A disastrous failure, indicated by rolling one or more 1s and no successes on the dice rolled for an action.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on the V20 inconsistency: the V20 has been made after a lot of years, during which the term &quot;botch&quot; started referring also to the singular die, even if nowhere in the rule it is stated like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T19:25:02-07:00","id":1558862,"title":"","content":"1s cancel successes, but soak and damage rolls can't have a final result of a botch.<br /> <br /> That's pretty consistent, esp. if you look past VtM.<br /> <br /> The big change was the &quot;general rule&quot; from 2nd to Rev that took away botching from rolling more 1s than successes.<br /> <br /> This is frequently house ruled for a number of reasons, and plenty of people have been playing with ignoring the special rules for rolling 1s on damage and soak for long enough that it can be forgotten that it's a house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T13:41:14-07:00","id":1561842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Submariner93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558861-2nd-revised-v20-damage-soak-and-1s#post1558861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion on the V20 inconsistency:</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an inconsistency. V20 changed several minor rules, it isn't only commemorative material, it's a new edition with some rules revision.<br /> <br /> And as Heavy Arms said, this particular rule has been commonly played as stated in V20 at least since Revised. I personally don't know or heard about a single group that counted 1s in damage and soak.<br /> <br /> Can't say from the top of my head, but some rules also started in supplements or other lines, that was not uncommon. So it may have started to be officially stated somewhere else in Revised or 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T14:08:23-07:00","id":1561844,"title":"","content":"Maybe the assumption comes from <i>Exalted</i>? I'm fairly sure a similar rule exists in Ex3, because I got exasperated that one type of damage doesn't count 1s, and another does, which is needlessly fiddly (Ex3's motto, probably).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}